            <ArticleTitle>Liquid Temperature Measurements Using Two Different Tunable Hollow Prisms.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">E266</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/s17020266</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes the design, fabrication, and testing of two hollow prisms. One is a prism with a grating glued to its hypotenuse. This ensemble, prism + grating, is called a grism. It can be applied as an on-axis tunable spectrometer. The other hollow prism is a constant deviation one called a Pellin-Broca. It can be used as a tunable dispersive element in a spectrometer with no moving parts. The application of prisms as temperature sensors is shown.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
